uity instead  basically being taken in by Batman and  befriending Batman's allies Harper Row  and Stephanie brown now orphan is an  incredibly skilled fighter arguably the  most skilled of the bat family with the  possible exception of Damian Wayne  largely due to her ability to anticipate  the moves of her opponents as well as  for extremely high pain tolerance and so  finally we have Stephanie Brown who  first appeared in a Detective Comics at  number 647 in 1992 Stephanie is the  daughter of the supervillain cluemaster  who begins working as a vigilante by the  name spoiler because of our mission to  spoil her father's plants now when Tim  Drake temporarily steps away from his  role as Robin to try and live in  life Stephanie fills the void but it's  tortured and apparently killed by the  black mask now it's later revealed that  Stephanie's death was faked and that  after the apparent death of Bruce Wayne  Cassandra Cain gives her Batgirl costume  to Stephanie who adopts the mantle  giving her the distinction of being the  only person to serve as both Robin and  Batgirl now in the new 52 continuity  we've only ever seen Stephanie in her  original spoiler persona and Stephanie  is a skilled martial artist and  acrobatic and is set apart by her  expertise as a tracker and so in  addition to all the Robins and all the  bad girls there are a few other members  of the bat family that we need to go  over to get a definitive answer as to  who would win in this gigantic Battle  Royale  now the first of these is jean-paul  Valley also known as Azrael who first  appeared in Batman sort of Azrael number  one in 1992 now Jean Paul was part of  the sacred order of st. Dumas a secret  order of assassins who was brainwashed  into forgetting the fact that his father  had died and it was time for him to take  over for him  at which point his memory was restored  now he fights alongside Batman and  becomes an apprentice of sorts until  Batman is paralyzed by Bane and Azrael  takes